{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "jsx": "preserve"
  },
  // `vueCompilerOptions.strictTemplates` is still OFF, and this comment is the
  // reason plus the measurement. Turning it on activates TreeUI's
  // `GlobalComponents` augmentation, which is what makes `vue-tsc` catch a prop
  // that does not exist (`<TTag clickable>`, `<TStat :hint>` — real bugs here
  // that cost translated copy and an accessible name). Vue drops an unknown prop
  // in silence, so without this the compiler agrees with every typo.
  //
  // Measured in this tree, not estimated, with vue-tsc 3.3.8:
  //   @treeui/vue 0.28.0 -> 89 errors (2 real, 87 library type friction)
  //   @treeui/vue 0.29.0 -> 50
  //   @treeui/vue 0.31.0 -> 12
  // What 0.31 closed: the element-attribute allowlist (`min`/`max` on a numeric
  // TInput, `readonly`, `href` on `TButton as="a"` — 17 -> 0) and the wide-model
  // asymmetry in the components that went generic, TInput/TTabs/TToggleGroup
  // (33 -> 0). The one error that was OURS is fixed: TToggleGroup takes its
  // options as `NoInfer`, so a bare literal had to be annotated.
  //
  // The remaining 12 are both library-side, both the same two shapes as before,
  // in components the first round did not cover:
  //   11  TSelect — `modelValue: string | number` and an emit of the same union,
  //       so a narrow ref (`ref<string>`, `ref<FilterType>`,
  //       `ref<'RequestResponse' | 'Event'>`) cannot be bound. Identical to the
  //       group the generics fixed elsewhere.
  //    1  TTextarea — `spellcheck` is outside the declared attribute surface
  //       (`readonly`/`rows`/`minlength`/`maxlength`/`autocomplete` are in it).
  //       It is a real `<textarea>` attribute and a JSON editor wants it off.
  // None of the 12 is a runtime bug. Turn this on when they close — and then
  // this comment goes with it.
  "include": [
    "src/**/*.ts",
    "src/**/*.tsx",
    "src/**/*.vue"
  ],
  // The root tsconfig excludes "src/ui" (so the server/client projects never
  // pull the dashboard in), and `exclude` is INHERITED by every config that
  // extends it — with paths resolved against the ROOT file. Left alone, that
  // excluded this whole directory from its own project and `vue-tsc --noEmit`
  // silently checked nothing. Reset it here.
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"],
  "references": [
    {
      "path": "./tsconfig.node.json"
    }
  ]
}
